{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (NURSE): Morning. Blood pressure while you wait, one twenty-eight over seventy-eight, pulse seventy-two. Doctor's just finishing up.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Ta.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (NURSE): M4 was a proper mess, forty minutes from Blacktown. You get caught?",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): Nah.",
  "[SEG0005] person_3 (DOCTOR): G'day, Dr Okonkwo. Sorry about the wait, we're heaving today. What's brought you in?",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): Elbow.",
  "[SEG0007] person_3 (DOCTOR): Which arm, and where on it?",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (PATIENT): Right, outer, six weeks, on and off. Like a hot nail.",
  "[SEG0009] person_3 (DOCTOR): Mainly when you load the arm?",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0011] person_3 (DOCTOR): Which jobs set it off?",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (PATIENT): Lifting a cup sets it off. Brushwork too.",
  "[SEG0013] person_3 (DOCTOR): Painter or carpenter?",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (PATIENT): Painter. Full time.",
  "[SEG0015] person_3 (DOCTOR): Up ladders a fair bit?",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0017] person_3 (DOCTOR): Err, quick side track, you see the cricket in that heat on the weekend?",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah. Couldn't hear myself think. Neighbour had the commentary blasting.",
  "[SEG0019] person_3 (DOCTOR): Full bore, was it? Grandkids around for the holidays too?",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (PATIENT): Two. One of each.",
  "[SEG0021] person_3 (DOCTOR): Ha, bet the house is loud. Mine were in the pool all arvo. Right, umm, back to the elbow.",
  "[SEG0022] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any fevers?",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0024] person_3 (DOCTOR): Weight up or down lately?",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (PATIENT): Dunno. Maybe. Belt's the same.",
  "[SEG0026] person_3 (DOCTOR): Cough, or shortness of breath?",
  "[SEG0027] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0028] person_3 (DOCTOR): And waterworks all fine?",
  "[SEG0029] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0030] person_3 (DOCTOR): Sleeve up. I'm on the lateral epicondyle, that outer bump. Sore there?",
  "[SEG0031] person_2 (PATIENT): Yep.",
  "[SEG0032] person_3 (DOCTOR): Fist, and extend the wrist against me. Same spot?",
  "[SEG0033] person_2 (PATIENT): Yep.",
  "[SEG0034] person_3 (DOCTOR): Hmm, let me think. No swelling, the elbow moves freely with no catch, tenderness is right over the lateral epicondyle, and resisted wrist extension reproduces the pain. That reads as lateral epicondylitis, tennis elbow from the grip rather than tennis, provisional but it fits. I wouldn't scan you today.",
  "[SEG0035] person_3 (DOCTOR): What have you been using on it?",
  "[SEG0036] person_2 (PATIENT): Umm. Neurofen. Two.",
  "[SEG0037] person_3 (DOCTOR): So ibuprofen, two of the two-hundred milligram tablets, four hundred milligrams when it's bad?",
  "[SEG0038] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0039] person_3 (DOCTOR): I'd hold the cortisone injection for now, so get a counterforce brace and wear it for gripping, and I'll refer you to physio for eccentric wrist work. Have that four hundred of ibuprofen with food, not on an empty stomach. If it's not settling after the physio we might inject it then. I'll see you back in six weeks."
 ],
